1  VARIANCE DECOMPOSITION
megascale: 271231 measurements, 76.9% negative before mapping, proline median +1.601 against +0.476 overall

--- measured folding stability, the twelve core substitutions ---
    cell value is the mean cost of that substitution in that domain, minus the domain's own baseline
    cells 1811 over 12 substitutions and 297 proteins, median cell n = 5
    between-substitution variance    0.02560  (sd 0.160)
    protein-by-substitution variance 0.06308  (sd 0.251)
    mean sampling variance           0.06687  (sd 0.259)
    SHARE ATTRIBUTABLE TO THE SUBSTITUTION: 29%

--- transferability, measured folding stability, the twelve core substitutions ---
    leave-one-protein-out, 1811 cells
    Pearson r = +0.289, R squared = 0.084, Spearman rho = +0.163

--- measured folding stability, all substitution classes ---
    cells 44557 over 361 substitutions and 298 proteins, median cell n = 4
    between-substitution variance    0.29490  (sd 0.543)
    protein-by-substitution variance 0.09552  (sd 0.309)
    mean sampling variance           0.14924  (sd 0.386)
    SHARE ATTRIBUTABLE TO THE SUBSTITUTION: 76%

--- transferability, all substitution classes ---
    leave-one-protein-out, 44557 cells
    Pearson r = +0.689, R squared = 0.475, Spearman rho = +0.680

--- transferability, transmembrane cohort, the twelve core substitutions ---
    leave-one-protein-out, 5790 cells
    Pearson r = +0.598, R squared = 0.358, Spearman rho = +0.593

--- transmembrane cohort, the twelve core substitutions ---
    cell value is the mean pathogenicity score of that substitution in that protein, minus the protein's own baseline mean
    cells 5790 over 12 substitutions and 501 proteins, median cell n = 16
    between-substitution variance    0.00767  (sd 0.088)
    protein-by-substitution variance 0.00612  (sd 0.078)
    mean sampling variance           0.00676  (sd 0.082)
    SHARE ATTRIBUTABLE TO THE SUBSTITUTION: 56%

====================================================================================================
2  THE SUBSTITUTION AGAINST THE POSITION
Held-out domains, 5 folds. The position signal is the mean measured cost of
every other substitution at the same position, which bounds what any
position-specific predictor could extract from that position.

--- all substitution classes, 271181 held-out measurements ---
    predictor                          Spearman     R squared   
    substitution identity alone        +0.479        0.264
    position signal alone              +0.742        0.570
    both together                      +0.779        0.653
    what the substitution adds on top of the position: +0.084 R squared
    what the position adds on top of the substitution: +0.390 R squared

--- the twelve core substitutions, 11111 held-out measurements ---
    predictor                          Spearman     R squared   
    substitution identity alone        +0.168        0.042
    position signal alone              +0.705        0.512
    both together                      +0.722        0.555
    what the substitution adds on top of the position: +0.043 R squared
    what the position adds on top of the substitution: +0.513 R squared

